[1m[38;5;231mSection 3 — which tooling should the spec set up from the start?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m Unit tests, node --test (Recommended)
  [38;5;246mZero-dependency runner plus the test cases above, written before the module. Keeps the repo dependency-free.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [ ] ESLint + Prettier
  [38;5;246mStandard JS lint and auto-format. Adds the repo's first dependency tree; worth it if the app will grow.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] End-to-end tests
  [38;5;246mPlaywright driving the real login form in a browser. Heavy for one stubbed form, but catches the DOM wiring.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] None of these
  [38;5;246mSkip test and tooling setup entirely; ship the module and the app.js changes on their own.[39m
